# Line-ending and binary policy.
#
# Why this file exists: this repo is edited on Windows, where git is
# configured with core.autocrlf=true, but every file ships to a Linux
# container. Without the rules below, a fresh clone or any `git checkout`
# on Windows rewrites run.sh with CRLF line endings. The release zip is
# built from the working tree, so that CRLF would reach HAOS, and a
# `#!/usr/bin/with-contenv bashio` shebang followed by CR does not execute.
# Nothing was corrupted when this file was added; the trap had simply not
# been triggered yet.

# Default: let git detect, and normalise text to LF in the repository.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Everything that runs inside the container must keep LF on checkout.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf

# Documentation. LF keeps diffs clean across platforms.
*.md            text eol=lf

# Binary artifacts. Never apply line-ending conversion or text diffing to
# these. The audit reports and the archived release zips are the records
# CLAUDE.md rule 1 and the repository notes depend on.
*.pdf           binary
*.zip           binary
*.docx          binary
*.xlsx          binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
